Step past the whole argument of an unknown macro in tools:::permissify(),
so the rd target stops timing out on deeply nested unknown macros.

parse_Rd(permissive = TRUE) turns each unknown macro and its {} arguments
into text.  permissify() (src/library/tools/R/parseRd.R) splices the
argument's elements in between "{" and "}" and then advances by 3, which
lands inside the spliced elements unless the argument had exactly one.
The outer loop then permissifies the nested contents again, which is
quadratic in the nesting depth (204,796 calls for oss-fuzz testcase
5796296471150592, 741 levels deep), and the inner loop no longer sees an
argument that follows, whose braces are dropped.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #548 (no Bugzilla report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/library/tools/R/parseRd.R
+++ b/src/library/tools/R/parseRd.R
@@ -229,13 +229,16 @@ permissify <- function(Rd)
    	    Rd[[i]] <- tagged(Rd[[i]], "TEXT", utils::getSrcref(Rd[[i]]))
             while (i < length(tags)) {
 		if (tags[i+1] == "LIST") {
+		    arg <- permissify(Rd[[i+1]])
 		    Rd <- c(Rd[seq_len(i)],
                             list(tagged("{", "TEXT", utils::getSrcref(Rd[[i+1]]))),
-                            permissify(Rd[[i+1]]),
+                            arg,
                             list(tagged("}", "TEXT", utils::getSrcref(Rd[[i+1]]))),
 			    Rd[seq_along(Rd)[-seq_len(i+1)]])
 		    tags <- RdTags(Rd)
-		    i <- i+3
+		    ## c() spliced the argument's elements in: step to its
+		    ## closing brace, past what permissify() has just done
+		    i <- i + 2L + length(arg)
 		} else if (tags[i+1] == "TEXT" && grepl("^ *$", Rd[[i+1]]))
 		    i <- i + 1
 		else
